{
 "_what": "The prospective holdout, drawn 2026-11-04 by `sample_holdout.py` under the protocol in docs/benchmarks/7b-holdout-protocol.md. Unlabelled: these are the questions, and the owner's answers are the answer key.",
 "_why": "Every vision benchmark in this project was scored against labels a Claude model wrote. The strongest result, 40 of 40 for Claude Sonnet, was measured against an answer key written by another Claude model - which measures agreement at least as much as correctness, and the report says so. Nothing can be promoted until somebody independent has checked the answers, and the owner is the only somebody available.",
 "_the_other_problem_this_fixes": "Three of five fields could not be measured at all on the spent corpus: piano had 4 and 6 negatives, hands 7 and 3, text overlay 11 and 1. A concert pianist's videos contain pianos and hands. With three negatives the only attainable specificities are 0, 0.33, 0.67 and 1.00, so a bar of 0.80 can be met only by a perfect score and one borderline video decides it. This draw is stratified across the detector's whole score range, deliberately including the strata where it is most confident, because that is where its false positives live.",
 "blind": true,
 "_blind_means": "No model answer is sent to the interface for these, and no score. A labeller who knows what the detector said is no longer an independent labeller.",
 "seed": 20261027,
 "drawn_on": "2026-11-04",
 "stratify_on": "piano_or_keyboard_visible",
 "fields": [
  "piano_or_keyboard_visible",
  "hands_visible",
  "text_overlay_present"
 ],
 "scope_rule": "Judge only what you can see in the frames shown. Not what you know about the video, not what is probably just off screen - what is visible.",
 "definitions": {
  "piano_or_keyboard_visible": "The KEYS have to be visible. A piano lid, a stool, or a player obviously at an instrument whose keys are out of shot is a no.",
  "hands_visible": "At least one hand, recognisably a hand. A forearm disappearing out of frame is a no.",
  "text_overlay_present": "Words placed on the video, not words that are part of the scene - sheet music, a poster on the wall and a logo on a piano are all no."
 },
